description:
Translate text to International Morse code (ITU-R M.1677-1) or Morse back to text. Letters are separated by spaces and words by ' / '. Wrap prosigns in angle brackets (<SOS>, <AR>, <SK>). Also returns the transmission time at a given speed in words per minute, with optional Farnsworth spacing. Same rules as redbison.dev/morse-code-translator.

Returns: Text: the Morse or decoded text. structuredContent { direction, morse | text, unsupported[] | unknownCodes[], durationSeconds, unitMs }.
Example input: {"input":"SOS at 18 wpm","direction":"encode","wpm":18}
